{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDmVJTaL61yALkWxGGt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied in `money.py`. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the shares always add up to the total.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\nThe leftover grosze go one each to the first people in the list. I tried a few cases and every one summed to the total: `(101,3)` gives `[34,34,33]`, `(99,3)` gives `[33,33,33]`, `(5,7)` gives `[1,1,1,1,1,0,0]`, and `(-100,3)` gives `[-33,-33,-34]`. The 3 existing tests in `test_money.py` pass. pytest isn't installed, so I ran them with `unittest`.\n\nTwo things before you ship:\n- **Who pays the extra grosz:** the first people in the list always get it. If the order is fixed, the same person pays it on every bill. That's fine for a hotfix, but check it's acceptable for the product.\n- **Regression test:** no test covers the uneven split yet. The two-line test `assertEqual(sum(split_cents(100, 3)), 100)` would stop this bug coming back, and I can add it now if you want. Otherwise it goes on next sprint's list.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Say if you want me to commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":18653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":429},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d3cf230-e137-4275-86f8-5fd86da36cd4","uuid":"f3213d5f-726c-45c0-8982-b8807be7b0a7","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:20:34.527Z","request_id":"req_011CggDmV3aqgqDHQ9xVqZiC"}
